<SddInterviewProtocol keywords="interview, coverage-map, sequential-questions, one-question-per-message, ask-tool, defaults-first, thread-pulling, stakes-split, next-step-menu, sdd-interview-protocol" type="directive" ver="1.0">
  <DirectiveContext>
    <Mission>
      Run ONE operator interview for an authoring step, and render the end-of-step handoff menu.
      Loaded lazily by a calling directive (discovery STEP_2–STEP_6, module-decomposition STEP_1–STEP_5,
      future authoring steps); the caller supplies the scope-type + its focus and stays the owner of
      what gets written. The protocol owns HOW questions reach the operator: the coverage map, the
      round loop, the one-question-per-message format, the AskUserQuestion binding, and the
      «что дальше» menu format. The caller's BeliefState keeps the beliefs (operator safeguard,
      dialogue discipline, diverge-before-recommend, language/style axioms) — this file inherits
      them and MUST NOT restate them.

      Input — scope-type, calling-step focus, intake gathered so far. Output — a closed coverage
      map + captured answers and decisions, returned to the calling step. This directive writes no
      artifact; control returns to the caller at CLOSE.
    </Mission>
  </DirectiveContext>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_OPERATOR_DIALOGUE_STYLE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE, AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION, AX_OPERATOR_OUTPUT_LIVE_TEXT">
    <Axiom id="AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE">
      The interview runs on a prepared channel — the coverage map: topics assembled BEFORE the first
      question from the caller's focus + `TopicCatalog`, each `✔` closed · `▶` in progress ·
      `␣` open · `✗ skip: <причина>` (notation per `COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT`). The interview ends when the map is closed — never when a
      question count is reached. After EVERY operator answer re-check the map: an answer that opens
      a new hole or risk ADDS a topic or reopens a closed one (thread-pulling per the caller's
      `AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD`); the question total the operator sees grows honestly with it. A skip
      on a high-stakes topic goes through `H_HIGH_STAKES_SKIP`.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_STAKES_SPLIT">
      The stakes of a question pick its delivery form (stakes defined by the caller's
      `AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE`):
      - **Развилка** (design, architecture, delivery boundary, trust boundary, irreversible or
        hard-to-undo choice) → ONE question per message, full form per `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT`,
        answered via ASK before the next question is composed.
      - **Default confirmation** (naming, a low-risk default, a yes/no with an obvious answer) →
        batched: up to 4 in one `AskUserQuestion` call, or a one-line «годится?» tail on a card.
      Unsure which it is → treat as развилка. Never bury a genuine fork inside a batch.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL">
      Развилки go strictly one at a time: compose Q(n+1) ONLY after the answer to Q(n) is in.
      Each next question MUST account for all previous answers — a question whose premises an
      earlier answer already invalidated is a protocol defect, not a style issue. The «Вопрос X из Y»
      counter is owned HERE (the format contract just renders it): X = порядковый номер вопроса в
      этом интервью, Y = вопросы уже заданные + развилки, ещё запланированные из открытых тем карты;
      when thread-pulling adds a topic, Y grows and the change is visible in the map line — never
      silently.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_DEFAULTS_FIRST">
      Where a defensible default exists, lead with it: «🎯 Куда клонюсь» names one concrete option
      and why it fits THIS task. The default MUST be the result of the caller's
      `AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND` search — never the first typical answer. Reserve open questions
      for decisions that are genuinely operator-owned (business goals, risk acceptance, priorities).
      On high-stakes questions the lean is stated but variants are presented without pre-anchoring —
      the operator picks.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_ASK_TOOL_BINDING">
      Every развилка ends in an `AskUserQuestion` call. Binding rules:
      - The chat message carries the full material (per `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT`); the ASK carries
        only short labels + one-line descriptions. Never move the argument into the ASK.
      - Options appear in the ASK in the SAME order they were printed in the chat message.
      - When a recommendation exists, print it FIRST in the chat message too (letter A) with
        «(рекомендую)» in its ASK label — printed order and recommended-first then coincide.
      - «Other» is provided by the tool automatically — never add your own.
      - Tool unavailable → drop ONLY the ASK call: a развилка message keeps
        `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT` and the answer arrives as free text; low-stakes batches fall back
        to the caller's plain-text question format when it defines one (e.g. discovery
        `QUESTION_FORMAT`), otherwise a compact numbered list.
      Batched default-confirmations use one ASK call with 2–4 questions.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_VISUAL_WHEN_RELATIONAL">
      When the subject of a question is relational — a flow, a boundary, a structure, a lifecycle,
      variants that differ in shape — draw a compact ASCII picture BEFORE the variants, per
      `ai/directives/sdd/visual-vocabulary.xml` (chat forms; ≤7 nodes; one diagram — one idea).
      A question about a single scalar choice stays text. The same relations later land in the
      spec's «Diagrams» section as mermaid — the chat ASCII is the operator's preview of them.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_SCANNABLE_TEXT">
      The operator surfs the message, they do not wade through it. Bold marks the load-bearing
      words inside bullets (the thing to notice, not whole sentences); each block opens with its
      emoji anchor (📌 ⚖️ 🎯); paragraphs stay ≤3 lines; no monolithic text walls. Emotion is
      seasoning, not paint — anchors and an occasional marker, never emoji on every line. The word
      «фактура» is banned in operator-facing text — say «что известно» / «данные».
    </Axiom>
  </BeliefState>

  <TopicCatalog>
    Base topics — every interview starts with these (map labels in Russian):

    | Topic | Substance |
    |---|---|
    | Цель и не-цель | what this step delivers; what it explicitly refuses to do in this iteration |
    | Потребители | who consumes the result and what they expect from it |
    | Слабые места | MANDATORY: holes, contradictions, unstated expectations of the intake — name them, per caller's `AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD` |
    | Внешние зависимости | what outside this scope must exist / hold for the design to stand |
    | Глубокие блоки | closed triage: external users/data? load that shapes design? persisted state? must be diagnosable in production? — a «yes» opens a dedicated topic in the map (security / нагрузка / хранение / наблюдаемость), dug within normal rounds |

    scope-type block — append per the caller's scope-type:

    | scope-type | Topics |
    |---|---|
    | product | Пользователи (who exactly) · Метрика успеха/провала (both) · Зачем сейчас · Worst case (who pays for it) |
    | library | Разработчики-потребители (which teams / repos) · DX (how consumption should feel; feeds Golden DX) · Версии (compatibility promises) |
    | infrastructure | Окружения (dev / CI / prod parity) · Доставка (how changes reach consumers) |
    | contracts | Стороны контракта (producers and consumers, who owns the schema) · Эволюция (changing without breaking consumers) |

    The calling step MAY narrow or extend the block for its focus (e.g. discovery STEP_3 keeps only
    what the Requirements Gate still misses); «Слабые места» stays on every map.
  </TopicCatalog>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_HIGH_STAKES_SKIP` | Operator insists on skipping an unclosed high-stakes topic — name the concrete cost; on a confirmed skip record `✗ skip: <причина>` in the map and proceed |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_1_INIT_MAP">
      <Goal>Build the coverage map — the prepared channel.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Assemble the map: base topics + the scope-type block from `TopicCatalog`, narrowed /
        extended by the calling step's focus. Mark topics the intake already answers `✔` — ask
        only what a decision still needs. Plan the first round (3–5 развилки max) from the open
        topics. The map line opens every question message (per `COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT`); no separate
        «here is my plan» narration.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_ROUNDS">
      <Goal>Close the map, one question at a time.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Loop until the map is closed (`AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE`); per question:
        1. Pick the next open topic; mark `▶`.
        2. Split by stakes (`AX_STAKES_SPLIT`): развилка → one message per
           `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT` + one `AskUserQuestion`; default confirmations → collect and
           batch (2–4 per ASK call).
        3. After each answer: update the map, pull the thread (`AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE`) — a new
           hole becomes a new topic and Y grows; compose the NEXT question in the light of ALL
           answers so far (`AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL`).
        4. A skip request on a high-stakes topic → `H_HIGH_STAKES_SKIP`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_CLOSE">
      <Goal>Verify closure and return to the caller.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Gate per `AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE`: every topic `✔` or `✗ skip: <причина>`. Show the
        final map + a compact digest of answers and decisions (Russian), including skips with
        reasons. Hand the digest to the calling step — it owns the Approval Check, artifact
        writing, and Decision Log entries. The caller's FINAL step (artifact written) renders the
        handoff menu per `NEXT_STEP_MENU_FORMAT`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <OutputContracts>
    <Contract id="COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT">
      One line, opens every question message. Topic labels in Russian; ≤72 columns; statuses:
      `✔` closed · `▶` in progress · `␣` open · `✗ skip: <причина>`.

      Карта: цель ✔ · потребители ✔ · **офлайн ▶** · зависимости ␣ · слабые места ␣

      The topic in progress is bold. The map is session state for the dialogue — it never lands in
      the spec.
    </Contract>

    <Contract id="QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT">
      The развилка message — «журнал с якорями». Live markdown, never fenced. Blocks in order;
      skip a block only when genuinely empty:

      1. Coverage map line (per `COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT`).
      2. `## Вопрос <X> из <Y> · <тема без вопросительного знака>` — X/Y per `AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL`.
      3. `**Решаем одной строкой:** <the fork, one sentence>`.
      4. ASCII diagram — only when the subject is relational (`AX_VISUAL_WHEN_RELATIONAL`).
      5. `**📌 Что известно**` — 2–5 bullets; load-bearing words bold; facts specific to THIS
         question, not a restate of the session.
      6. `**⚖️ Варианты**` — each variant:
         `**<Letter>. <название>**` then `✅ <плюсы через · >` / `⚠️ <минусы через · >`.
         3+ variants with comparable criteria → a criteria×variant table INSTEAD of the lists
         (rows = criteria, columns = variants; the killer cell bold).
      7. `**🎯 Куда клонюсь:** <letter> — <why, one sentence>` — omit on high-stakes questions
         where pre-anchoring is wrong (`AX_DEFAULTS_FIRST`).
      8. The `AskUserQuestion` call (`AX_ASK_TOOL_BINDING`) — options in printed order.

      <Example>
        Карта: цель ✔ · потребители ✔ · **офлайн ▶** · зависимости ␣ · слабые места ␣

        ## Вопрос 3 из 5 · Что происходит с сообщением, отправленным без сети

        **Решаем одной строкой:** куда девается исходящее сообщение, пока сети нет — и что видит пользователь.

        ```
        [набрал текст] ──отправить──► ??? ──сеть вернулась──► [доставлено]
                                       │
                              что здесь: очередь? блок? потеря?
        ```

        **📌 Что известно**
        - Пользователь **не отличает** «нет сети» от «медленно» — Telegram и Slack кладут сообщение в ленту сразу, с часиками.
        - У нас уже есть outbox — очередь с **ретраями на реконнекте**.
        - Потеря набранного текста — **худший исход**: хуже, чем дубль.

        **⚖️ Варианты**

        **A. Сразу в ленту, отправка фоном через outbox**
        ✅ привычно по Telegram/Slack · текст не теряется · outbox уже есть
        ⚠️ нужна честная пометка статуса, иначе «отправилось?» — тикеты в поддержку

        **B. Блокировать отправку, пока нет сети**
        ✅ никакой двусмысленности статуса
        ⚠️ текст в заложниках у сети · ни один живой мессенджер так не делает

        **🎯 Куда клонюсь:** A — очередь уже есть, остаётся статус в UI.

        (AskUserQuestion: «A. В ленту + фон (рекомендую)» · «B. Блокировать отправку»)
      </Example>
    </Contract>

    <Contract id="BATCH_CONFIRM_FORMAT">
      Default confirmations — one compact block, then ONE `AskUserQuestion` call with 2–4
      questions. Per item: one bold line (the default) + one plain line (the alternative and when
      it wins). No «Что известно» blocks, no diagrams. A batch item that provokes discussion is
      promoted to a развилка next message.
    </Contract>

    <Contract id="NEXT_STEP_MENU_FORMAT">
      Rendered by the CALLER's final step, after its artifact is written and verified. Shape:

      1. One ✅ line — what was produced and what was checked
         (`✅ Спека <path> записана · язык проверен · <N> диаграмм`).
      2. `**Что дальше?**` + one `AskUserQuestion` call. Options (2–4) come from the caller's own
         candidate table; the recommended option first with «(рекомендую)»; CHAINED options are
         first-class («декомпозиция + критик следом», «scaffold + критик», «сразу execute») — one
         pick launches the whole chain, the agent runs it без промежуточных остановок between
         chain links unless a link fails. Always include «Закончить сессию» last.
      3. On pick: invoke the corresponding skill(s) / directive flow(s) directly — never answer
         with «запусти /sdd-X сам».
    </Contract>
  </OutputContracts>
</SddInterviewProtocol>
